{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dependable-unbeloved-leonberger","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nplan_review_T1.md instructs \"Tool-grounded where possible (web/codebase)\", but the agent toolset (src/rebar/llm/pai_tools.py, wired at src/rebar/llm/runner.py:257) provides only read_file, list_directory, search_files, resolve_symbol, show_ticket — no web access. Empirically only 3/14 recent T1 findings were tool-grounded; the rubric's primary grounding channel is dead weight. Operator ruled this a bug.\n\n## Approach\nEnable Anthropic's server-side web-search tool for AGENT criteria that declare it: add an optional `\"web\": true` key to a criterion's routing entry (T1 only, initially); when set and the resolved provider is anthropic, the runner adds the server-side web_search tool to that request's model settings (seam: src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py settings assembly, alongside the existing cache settings at anthropic_model.py:39-52). Non-anthropic providers and offline runs get today's behavior; the T1 rubric is updated to say web grounding applies when the tool is offered and to fall back to codebase/plan reasoning otherwise. Alternative rejected: a homegrown HTTP fetch tool in pai_tools — network policy, sanitization, and result-quality burdens for one criterion when the provider offers a managed tool.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py, src/rebar/llm/runner.py (thread the per-request web flag), src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json (T1 entry), src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T1.md, tests/llm/test_web_tool_gating.py.\n\n## Testing\nUnit: a request flagged web=true on an anthropic-resolved model carries the web tool in settings; openai/gemini-resolved models do not; unflagged criteria never carry it. No live web call in tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A T1 pass-1 request against an anthropic-resolved model includes the server-side web-search tool in its model settings (checked: unit test on settings assembly).\n- [ ] Non-anthropic providers and non-web criteria produce byte-identical settings to today (checked: unit test comparison).\n- [ ] plan_review_T1.md describes the conditional availability and the fallback (checked: test asserts rubric text).","id":"ff64-ca12-7132-40e7","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"T1 prior-art rubric mandates web grounding but no web tool exists"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785384342781915001,"uuid":"23e06a8e-d2ea-4c63-bc17-442632f1b8b3"}